\]

**x‑direction**

\[
p_{x,\text{initial}} = m_1 u_{1x}=5\,(2)=10\ \text{kg·m/s}
\]

Final x‑component of velocity  

\[
v_x = \frac{p_{x,\text{initial}}}{M}= \frac{10}{15}=0.667\ \text{m/s}
\]

**y‑direction**

\[
p_{y,\text{initial}} = m_2 u_{2y}=10\,(4)=40\ \text{kg·m/s}
\]

Final y‑component of velocity  

\[
v_y = \frac{p_{y,\text{initial}}}{M}= \frac{40}{15}=2.667\ \text{m/s}
\]

**Resultant speed**

\[
v = \sqrt{v_x^{2}+v_y^{2}}
   = \sqrt{(0.667)^2+(2.667)^2}
   = \sqrt{0.444+7.111}
   = \sqrt{7.555}
   \approx 2.75\ \text{m/s}
\]

